  "title": "Achaemenid Empire",
  "summary": "The Achaemenid Persian Empire was founded by Cyrus the Great, who became king of Persis in 559 BCE, defeated Astyages of Media in 550 and captured Babylon in 539. Under Darius it stretched from Macedonia to Pakistan, with capitals at Pasargadae and Persepolis. It ended in 330 BCE after Alexander defeated Darius III at Issus and Gaugamela.",
